{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/postgres/postgres/compare/master...b63f25bddfebc67b1e78f86341a6aecb0e9fe576","html_url":"https://github.com/postgres/postgres/compare/master...b63f25bddfebc67b1e78f86341a6aecb0e9fe576","permalink_url":"https://github.com/postgres/postgres/compare/postgres:0dbe240...postgres:b63f25b","diff_url":"https://github.com/postgres/postgres/compare/master...b63f25bddfebc67b1e78f86341a6aecb0e9fe576.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/postgres/postgres/compare/master...b63f25bddfebc67b1e78f86341a6aecb0e9fe576.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"0dbe240dc0e14448fe82f6b356947d4b5c93f89f","node_id":"C_kwDOAA4m0toAKDBkYmUyNDBkYzBlMTQ0NDhmZTgyZjZiMzU2OTQ3ZDRiNWM5M2Y4OWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Paquier","email":"michael@paquier.xyz","date":"2026-11-12T22:54:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"Michael Paquier","email":"michael@paquier.xyz","date":"2026-11-12T22:54:35Z"},"message":"Fix some edge cases with characteristics after COMMIT/ROLLBACK AND CHAIN\n\nCertain combinations of transaction sequences with AND CHAIN failed to\npreserve the top-transaction characteristics, in some cases:\n* When a transaction block failed, the chained transaction used the\ndefault characteristics, not the characteristics of the transaction\nchaining from.\n* When COMMIT AND CHAIN was issued in a subtransaction that had the idea\nto switch read_only, the chained transaction inherited the read-only\nstate of the subtransaction, not of the top transaction.  The state is\nreset when the subtransaction ends, like RELEASE.  The characteristics\nare now saved once all the subtransactions are committed.\n\nNarek has reported the first problem.  I have discovered the second\npattern while digging through this area of the code.  Tests are added\nfor all the patterns spotted.\n\nAuthor: Narek Galstyan <narek.galstyan@enterprisedb.com>\nAuthor: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>\nDiscussion: https://postgr.es/m/CAHsn6_z-ewqXWe2h--SK93AdnPSOvjvF9KLodWckFZKAjxcONw@mail.gmail.com\nBackpatch-through: 15","tree":{"sha":"442d22d5d5077007a1e87c01f045e8d54b61111c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/postgres/postgres/git/trees/442d22d5d5077007a1e87c01f045e8d54b61111c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/postgres/postgres/git/commits/0dbe240dc0e14448fe82f6b356947d4b5c93f89f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/postgres/postgres/commits/0dbe240dc0e14448fe82f6b356947d4b5c93f89f","html_url":"https://github.com/postgres/postgres/commit/0dbe240dc0e14448fe82f6b356947d4b5c93f89f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/postgres/postgres/commits/0dbe240dc0e14448fe82f6b356947d4b5c93f89f/comments","author":{"login":"michaelpq","id":985332,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NTMzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/985332?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelpq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"michaelpq","id":985332,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NTMzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/985332?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelpq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7fffb114377507fca5e8c2b4db1820a4ec11615b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/postgres/postgres/commits/7fffb114377507fca5e8c2b4db1820a4ec11615b","html_url":"https://github.com/postgres/postgres/commit/7fffb114377507fca5e8c2b4db1820a4ec11615b"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"b63f25bddfebc67b1e78f86341a6aecb0e9fe576","node_id":"C_kwDOAA4m0toAKGI2M2YyNWJkZGZlYmM2N2IxZTc4Zjg2MzQxYTZhZWNiMGU5ZmU1NzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Paquier","email":"michael@paquier.xyz","date":"2026-05-11T12:13:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"Noah Misch","email":"noah@leadboat.com","date":"2026-05-11T12:13:46Z"},"message":"Fix unbounded recursive handling of SSL/GSS in ProcessStartupPacket()\n\nThe handling of SSL and GSS negotiation messages in\nProcessStartupPacket() could cause a recursion of the backend,\nultimately crashing the server as the negotiation attempts were not\ntracked across multiple calls processing startup packets.\n\nA malicious client could therefore alternate rejected SSL and GSS\nrequests indefinitely, each adding a stack frame, until the backend\ncrashed with a stack overflow, taking down a server.\n\nThis commit addresses this issue by modifying ProcessStartupPacket() so\nas processed negotiation attempts are tracked, preventing infinite\nrecursive attempts.  A TAP test is added to check this problem, where\nmultiple SSL and GSS negotiated attempts are stacked.\n\nReported-by: Calif.io in collaboration with Claude and Anthropic\nResearch\nAuthor: Michael Paquier <michael@paquier.xyz>\nReviewed-by: Daniel Gustafsson <daniel@yesql.se>\nSecurity: CVE-2026-6479\nBackpatch-through: 14","tree":{"sha":"6f81b1fd62877ca97df4020e70559783f0a66d3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/postgres/postgres/git/trees/6f81b1fd62877ca97df4020e70559783f0a66d3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/postgres/postgres/git/commits/b63f25bddfebc67b1e78f86341a6aecb0e9fe576","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/postgres/postgres/commits/b63f25bddfebc67b1e78f86341a6aecb0e9fe576","html_url":"https://github.com/postgres/postgres/commit/b63f25bddfebc67b1e78f86341a6aecb0e9fe576","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/postgres/postgres/commits/b63f25bddfebc67b1e78f86341a6aecb0e9fe576/comments","author":{"login":"michaelpq","id":985332,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NTMzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/985332?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelpq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelpq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"nmisch","id":5084293,"node_i